{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Connect to the tracking service, consume frames, and shut down cleanly."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"LeapSwift has one entry point: "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". Creating it opens a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"connection to the Ultraleap service and starts a background polling loop;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consuming ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController\/events","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" delivers everything that loop observes."}]},{"text":"Create a Controller","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Create-a-Controller"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController\/init(trackingMode:mock:mockScenario:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"async throws","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It throws a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapError","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" if the connection to the service cannot be created or opened —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"most often because the Ultraleap Hand Tracking service is not running."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import LeapSwift","","let controller = try await LeapController(trackingMode: .desktop)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tracking mode is applied once the service reports a connection, so there is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no need to wait for "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapEvent\/connected"},{"type":"text","text":" before setting it. To change it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"later, call "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController\/setTrackingMode(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Consume Events","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Consume-Events"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController\/events","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AsyncStream"},{"type":"text","text":" you can iterate from any task. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stream carries connection lifecycle events alongside tracking frames, so a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single loop can drive both your UI state and your hand rendering."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let task = Task {","    for await event in controller.events {","        switch event {","        case .connected:","            status = \"Connected\"","        case .disconnected:","            status = \"Service unavailable\"","        case .deviceFound:","            status = \"Device ready\"","        case .deviceLost:","            status = \"Device unplugged\"","        case .trackingFrame(let frame):","            render(frame)","        case .error(let error):","            log(error.localizedDescription)","        @unknown default:","            break","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapEvent","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is not "},{"code":"@frozen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so a ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" outside the framework needs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"code":"@unknown default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/HandType","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/VersionPart","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" are frozen and switch","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exhaustively without one.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Failures raised while the controller is handling an event cannot be thrown to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you, so they arrive as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapEvent\/error(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". The controller keeps running: it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stays connected and retries opening a device on the next "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapEvent\/connected","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapEvent\/deviceFound(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you only care about hand data, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController\/frames","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" maps the stream to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HandFrame?"},{"type":"text","text":", emitting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" for non-tracking events:"}]},{"code":["for await frame in controller.frames {","    guard let frame else { continue }","    render(frame)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"style":"important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The stream is unicast. Iterating "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController\/events","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" from two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"places splits the events between them rather than duplicating them. To fan out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to multiple consumers, iterate once and rebroadcast."}]}],"name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"text":"Detect a Gesture","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Detect-a-Gesture"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pinch and grab are reported per hand as normalized strengths, which is usually"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"easier to work with than raw joint positions."}]},{"code":["for await frame in controller.frames {","    guard let hand = frame?.rightHand else { continue }","","    if hand.grabStrength > 0.8 {","        beginDrag(at: hand.palm.position)","    } else if hand.pinchStrength > 0.9 {","        select(at: hand.index.tipPosition)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/Hand\/palm","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" also exposes "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/Palm\/stabilizedPosition","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", a time-filtered position"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that is better suited to pointing at 2D UI than the raw"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/Palm\/position","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/Hand\/isPinching","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" reflects the service’s own gesture flag, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requires a gesture detection license. Without one it stays "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; compare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/Hand\/pinchStrength","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/Hand\/pinchDistance"},{"type":"text","text":" against a threshold instead."}]}],"name":"Note","type":"aside"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Inspect-the-Device","text":"Inspect the Device"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Device details become available once a device has been opened, which happens"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"automatically after "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapEvent\/connected","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". Before that,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController\/deviceInfo()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["if let info = await controller.deviceInfo() {","    print(\"Serial: \\(info.serialNumber)\")","    print(\"FOV: \\(info.horizontalFOV) × \\(info.verticalFOV)\")","}","","let version = try await controller.version(of: .serverLibrary)","print(\"Service v\\(version.major).\\(version.minor).\\(version.patch)\")"]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Shut-Down","text":"Shut Down"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController\/stop()"},{"text":" cancels polling, finishes the event stream — which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends any ","type":"text"},{"code":"for await","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" loop over it — and closes the device and connection.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" performs the same teardown, so stopping explicitly is only necessary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"when you want tracking to end before the controller is released.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["await controller.stop()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Calling ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.studiomexx.LeapSwift\/documentation\/LeapSwift\/LeapController\/stop()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" more than once is safe. After stopping, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"controller cannot be reconnected; create a new one instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Starting-Without-a-Device","text":"Starting Without a Device"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything above needs the Ultraleap service and a physical device. If you","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"don’t have either handy — or want deterministic data for a demo or a test —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"mock: .always","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and get the exact same event stream from synthetic hand","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"data instead:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let con